63
00:05:40,781 --> 00:05:47,900
Fairchild Republic took on the challenges of designing an aircraft unlike any ever built.

64
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:56,200
The winning design would be a stable, straight-winged aircraft to allow for excellent lift and maneuverability.

65
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:05,720
This combined with the General Electric's TF-34 turbofan engines, which would give it a high thrust for takeoff

66
00:06:05,721 --> 00:06:12,600
and a low fuel consumption to enable the plane to have voider capabilities essential for the role.

67
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:22,040
With unbeatable durability and an easy-to-repair maintenance program,

68
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:26,140
these were the ideal engines designed to fly in a hostile battle zone.

69
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:33,620
But for the Fairchild team, the challenges became apparent immediately.

70
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:36,720
The typical way to build a jet airplane,

71
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:40,980
and the reason that all jet fighters are impossible to use in this close support mission,

72
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,620
