73
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:47,560
Once you have fuel wrapped around an engine, a .22 rifle will kill you.

74
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:52,940
One of our very first design rules was fuel had to be someplace other than the engine.

75
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:59,700
Not only was the fuel safely stored in the fuselage away from the engines,

76
00:06:59,701 --> 00:07:03,840
The fuel tanks also had unique built-in fire suppression capabilities.

77
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:13,580
The aircraft's hydraulics could also withstand serious firepower.

78
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:24,720
We required that every hydraulic control had to be backed up by a simple mechanical cable system that's much harder to shoot out.

79
00:07:24,721 --> 00:07:33,220
we could come back with hydraulic system shot out half the tail shot off a piece of the wing shot

