142
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:05,860
It was pretty awe-inspiring.

143
00:13:05,861 --> 00:13:10,480
It was so much bigger than the aircraft I'd flown in pilot training.

144
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:16,020
Just, it felt huge and it felt big getting into it.

145
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:19,780
And it was also intimidating just because the first time you fly the airplane, you're by yourself.

146
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:22,060
But it was definitely exhilarating at the same time.

147
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:31,480
The single-seat cockpit is surrounded by a large bubble canopy to provide all-around vision and a bulletproof windscreen.

148
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,580
I love single-seat cockpit.

149
00:13:34,581 --> 00:13:37,580
that's one of the reasons that I was enticed by the A-10.

150
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:41,660
No one looking over your shoulder, no one telling you what to do.

151
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:45,300
You put the aircraft where you want to do it and you employ it

152
00:13:45,301 --> 00:13:47,120
in the fashion that you want to employ it.

153
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:50,340
It's all personal, and you are the master.

154
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:56,120
I think the first time that was one of the things that surprised me.

155
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:59,040
It took itself right off the runway for the most part.

156
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:04,380
Once it hits the speed it wants to fly, it just lifts up and away.

157
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:11,580
I think it probably has to do a lot with the big straight wing, positive camber on the

158
00:14:11,581 --> 00:14:13,580
wing. It wants to fly.

159
00:14:13,581 --> 00:14:15,386
The plane reacts to you.

160
00:14:15,387 --> 00:14:20,580
It's like you kind of strap on the plane itself and it's an extension

161
00:14:20,581 --> 00:14:26,281
of you and it flies. It has a feel of a real stick and rudder.

162
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:28,580
The A-10 is known for its

163
00:14:28,581 --> 00:14:31,168
tight turn radius, so it can turn on a dime.

164
00:14:31,169 --> 00:14:33,580
You can even look at the ground as you're

165
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:35,580
and it looks like you're just turning in space.

166
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,580
Straight wing lets us turn very, very tight.

167
00:14:40,581 --> 00:14:43,580
So even though we're going slow, we've got a very small turn radius,

168
00:14:43,581 --> 00:14:46,580
and we can very quickly move our flight path

169
00:14:46,581 --> 00:14:51,580
