180
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:28,940
Their artillery can't get the enemy.

181
00:15:28,941 --> 00:15:30,420
They call in the AT&T.

182
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:35,080
Flying of the airplane has to become secondary.

183
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:38,760
Now you're trying to employ the weapon system, and that's where it gets complicated.

184
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:44,480
We get maps spread out in the cockpit, and we're still trying to talk on the radios and keep from getting shot at.

185
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:55,440
You know, we consider ourselves the last gunfighter that's really out there,

186
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:59,680
because when you go into battle and it's a close-in cast fight,

187
00:15:59,681 --> 00:16:03,120
the number one weapon of choice of an A-10 pilot is going to be their gun.

188
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:10,300
The weapons delivery system incorporates a heads-up display, or HUD,

189
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:14,320
that provides the pilot with the references for flight control and weapons employment.

190
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:24,060
It's incredibly accurate for a gun system and probably one of the most flexible weapon systems in the world.

191
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:27,860
It's just point and shoot, just like you'd imagine a revolver in your hand.

192
00:16:27,861 --> 00:16:31,800
You point it where you want to shoot it, you pull the trigger, and that's where the bullets are going to go.

193
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:38,540
When you roll in and you pull the trigger for the first time, you get excited,

194
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:45,620
and the adrenaline starts pumping through, and I had the biggest smile on my face.

195
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:50,140
What a feeling shooting the gun. I mean, the whole airplane shakes.

196
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:54,780
The first time I fired the gun, you know, I had to come off the trigger because it scared me,

197
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,340
because I couldn't believe something like that could come out of the front of the airplane,

198
00:16:57,341 --> 00:16:58,880
and all the flames, the smoke.

199
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:03,380
This 30-millimeter bullet is the size of my forearm.

200
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:08,380
And that smell of gunpowder, you get that in the cockpit after you fire the gun.

201
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:09,980
And it's just incredible.

202
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:13,260
You get a little bit of a high from it, I think, sometimes.

203
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,140
It smells like victory.

204
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:20,500
